{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These cases use one ownership model. Definitions describe chart behavior. CSS\nvariables supply inherited paint. Application shells compose cards and controls."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"cases","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cases"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Case"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Demonstrates"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/charts/120-themed-interactive-area/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Themed interactive area card"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A CSS-backed gradient, sparse guides, range controls, grouped focus, a tooltip, and keyed motion"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/charts/121-active-bar-dashboard/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Active bar dashboard"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Metric selectors around gradient bars, a focused band ring, a tooltip, and spring transitions"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/charts/122-premium-kpi-sparklines/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Premium KPI sparklines"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Three guide-free line and area hosts inside one responsive KPI grid"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/charts/123-active-donut-metric/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Active donut metric"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Native pie allocation, a selected wedge and ring, center text, legend state, and a CSS palette"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/charts/124-theme-palette-matrix/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Theme palette matrix"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One chart structure rendered through neutral, vibrant, and monochrome token sets"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"ownership","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ownership"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layer"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Owns"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Does not own"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rows, keys, marks, scales, guides, gradients, focus, tooltip policy, and motion timing"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Card layout, HTML controls, theme switching, or renderer selection"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CSS variables"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Paint tokens, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"currentColor"},{"type":"text","value":", tooltip chrome, and application surface colors"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Data meaning, scales, geometry, or selection"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"App shell"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Card layout, text, controls, selected state, theme class, and the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion()"},{"type":"text","value":" renderer"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mark geometry or duplicated SVG presentation"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memoize or recreate the definition when rows or semantic options change. A CSS\ntoken change does not require a new definition."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep each mark key stable across updates. The motion renderer uses stable keys\nfor DOM identity, presentation points, and spring velocity."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"motion-boundary","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Motion boundary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion"},{"type":"text","value":" value in a definition is inert policy. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion()"},{"type":"text","value":" as the\nrenderer to activate tween or spring transitions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default SVG renderer uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"svgAnimation"},{"type":"text","value":". The motion renderer ignores that\noption because each host has one animation owner. Static SVG and Canvas paint\nthe final state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion()"},{"type":"text","value":" respects reduced motion by default. React and Octane "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/core"},{"type":"text","value":" hosts\naccept an explicit renderer. Renderer-neutral DOM hosts accept one too. Other\nframework adapters currently expose their default SVG surface."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read "},{"type":"link","href":"../guides/dynamic-data-and-animation.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dynamic Data and Animation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and\nthe "},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/motion.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Motion reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for update and timing contracts."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"paint-boundary","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Paint boundary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use CSS variables when paint follows the application theme. Use a definition\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"theme"},{"type":"text","value":" for explicit scene defaults. Declare gradients in the definition so\nSVG and Canvas use the same resource."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a stable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idPrefix"},{"type":"text","value":" when several charts share a document. Keep card borders,\nshadows, layout, and non-chart text in the application shell."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read "},{"type":"link","href":"../guides/themes-and-styling.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Themes and Styling"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for palette,\ngradient, Canvas, and tooltip behavior."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"current-limits","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current limits"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chart specs declare linear and radial gradients, but they do not declare\npattern resources."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grid"},{"type":"text","value":" and the static axis line are visibility controls. They do not accept\nstroke width, dash, or opacity."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"theme.grid"},{"type":"text","value":" for shared guide paint. Use rule marks for styled static\nannotations and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"crosshair"},{"type":"text","value":" for styled focus guides."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"barX"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"barY"},{"type":"text","value":" accept one radius value for all rectangle corners. They do\nnot expose endpoint-only or per-corner radii."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The optional motion renderer targets browser SVG. Static SVG, Canvas, and\nnative surfaces consume the definitions but paint the final state."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"cases","text":"Cases","level":2},{"id":"ownership","text":"Ownership","level":2},{"id":"motion-boundary","text":"Motion boundary","level":2},{"id":"paint-boundary","text":"Paint boundary","level":2},{"id":"current-limits","text":"Current limits","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThese cases use one ownership model. Definitions describe chart behavior. CSS\nvariables supply inherited paint. Application shells compose cards and controls.\n\n## Cases\n\n| Case                                                                                                    | Demonstrates                                                                                     |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| [Themed interactive area card](https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/charts/120-themed-interactive-area/) | A CSS-backed gradient, sparse guides, range controls, grouped focus, a tooltip, and keyed motion |\n| [Active bar dashboard](https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/charts/121-active-bar-dashboard/)            | Metric selectors around gradient bars, a focused band ring, a tooltip, and spring transitions    |\n| [Premium KPI sparklines](https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/charts/122-premium-kpi-sparklines/)        | Three guide-free line and area hosts inside one responsive KPI grid                              |\n| [Active donut metric](https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/charts/123-active-donut-metric/)              | Native pie allocation, a selected wedge and ring, center text, legend state, and a CSS palette   |\n| [Theme palette matrix](https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/charts/124-theme-palette-matrix/)            | One chart structure rendered through neutral, vibrant, and monochrome token sets                 |\n\n## Ownership\n\n| Layer         | Owns                                                                                   | Does not own                                                       |\n| ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Definition    | Rows, keys, marks, scales, guides, gradients, focus, tooltip policy, and motion timing | Card layout, HTML controls, theme switching, or renderer selection |\n| CSS variables | Paint tokens, `currentColor`, tooltip chrome, and application surface colors           | Data meaning, scales, geometry, or selection                       |\n| App shell     | Card layout, text, controls, selected state, theme class, and the `motion()` renderer  | Mark geometry or duplicated SVG presentation                       |\n\nMemoize or recreate the definition when rows or semantic options change. A CSS\ntoken change does not require a new definition.\n\nKeep each mark key stable across updates. The motion renderer uses stable keys\nfor DOM identity, presentation points, and spring velocity.\n\n## Motion boundary\n\nA `motion` value in a definition is inert policy. Pass `motion()` as the\nrenderer to activate tween or spring transitions.\n\nThe default SVG renderer uses `svgAnimation`. The motion renderer ignores that\noption because each host has one animation owner. Static SVG and Canvas paint\nthe final state.\n\n`motion()` respects reduced motion by default. React and Octane `/core` hosts\naccept an explicit renderer. Renderer-neutral DOM hosts accept one too. Other\nframework adapters currently expose their default SVG surface.\n\nRead [Dynamic Data and Animation](../guides/dynamic-data-and-animation.md) and\nthe [Motion reference](../reference/motion.md) for update and timing contracts.\n\n## Paint boundary\n\nUse CSS variables when paint follows the application theme. Use a definition\n`theme` for explicit scene defaults. Declare gradients in the definition so\nSVG and Canvas use the same resource.\n\nUse a stable `idPrefix` when several charts share a document. Keep card borders,\nshadows, layout, and non-chart text in the application shell.\n\nRead [Themes and Styling](../guides/themes-and-styling.md) for palette,\ngradient, Canvas, and tooltip behavior.\n\n## Current limits\n\n- Chart specs declare linear and radial gradients, but they do not declare\n  pattern resources.\n- `grid` and the static axis line are visibility controls. They do not accept\n  stroke width, dash, or opacity.\n- Use `theme.grid` for shared guide paint. Use rule marks for styled static\n  annotations and `crosshair` for styled focus guides.\n- `barX` and `barY` accept one radius value for all rectangle corners. They do\n  not expose endpoint-only or per-corner radii.\n- The optional motion renderer targets browser SVG. Static SVG, Canvas, and\n  native surfaces consume the definitions but paint the final state.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Themes and Motion\ndescription: Apply inherited palettes and optional motion while keeping chart definitions separate from card layout and controls.\n---\n\nThese cases use one ownership model. Definitions describe chart behavior. CSS\nvariables supply inherited paint. Application shells compose cards and controls.\n\n## Cases\n\n| Case                                                                                                    | Demonstrates                                                                                     |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| [Themed interactive area card](https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/charts/120-themed-interactive-area/) | A CSS-backed gradient, sparse guides, range controls, grouped focus, a tooltip, and keyed motion |\n| [Active bar dashboard](https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/charts/121-active-bar-dashboard/)            | Metric selectors around gradient bars, a focused band ring, a tooltip, and spring transitions    |\n| [Premium KPI sparklines](https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/charts/122-premium-kpi-sparklines/)        | Three guide-free line and area hosts inside one responsive KPI grid                              |\n| [Active donut metric](https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/charts/123-active-donut-metric/)              | Native pie allocation, a selected wedge and ring, center text, legend state, and a CSS palette   |\n| [Theme palette matrix](https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/charts/124-theme-palette-matrix/)            | One chart structure rendered through neutral, vibrant, and monochrome token sets                 |\n\n## Ownership\n\n| Layer         | Owns                                                                                   | Does not own                                                       |\n| ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Definition    | Rows, keys, marks, scales, guides, gradients, focus, tooltip policy, and motion timing | Card layout, HTML controls, theme switching, or renderer selection |\n| CSS variables | Paint tokens, `currentColor`, tooltip chrome, and application surface colors           | Data meaning, scales, geometry, or selection                       |\n| App shell     | Card layout, text, controls, selected state, theme class, and the `motion()` renderer  | Mark geometry or duplicated SVG presentation                       |\n\nMemoize or recreate the definition when rows or semantic options change. A CSS\ntoken change does not require a new definition.\n\nKeep each mark key stable across updates. The motion renderer uses stable keys\nfor DOM identity, presentation points, and spring velocity.\n\n## Motion boundary\n\nA `motion` value in a definition is inert policy. Pass `motion()` as the\nrenderer to activate tween or spring transitions.\n\nThe default SVG renderer uses `svgAnimation`. The motion renderer ignores that\noption because each host has one animation owner. Static SVG and Canvas paint\nthe final state.\n\n`motion()` respects reduced motion by default. React and Octane `/core` hosts\naccept an explicit renderer. Renderer-neutral DOM hosts accept one too. Other\nframework adapters currently expose their default SVG surface.\n\nRead [Dynamic Data and Animation](../guides/dynamic-data-and-animation.md) and\nthe [Motion reference](../reference/motion.md) for update and timing contracts.\n\n## Paint boundary\n\nUse CSS variables when paint follows the application theme. Use a definition\n`theme` for explicit scene defaults. Declare gradients in the definition so\nSVG and Canvas use the same resource.\n\nUse a stable `idPrefix` when several charts share a document. Keep card borders,\nshadows, layout, and non-chart text in the application shell.\n\nRead [Themes and Styling](../guides/themes-and-styling.md) for palette,\ngradient, Canvas, and tooltip behavior.\n\n## Current limits\n\n- Chart specs declare linear and radial gradients, but they do not declare\n  pattern resources.\n- `grid` and the static axis line are visibility controls. They do not accept\n  stroke width, dash, or opacity.\n- Use `theme.grid` for shared guide paint. Use rule marks for styled static\n  annotations and `crosshair` for styled focus guides.\n- `barX` and `barY` accept one radius value for all rectangle corners. They do\n  not expose endpoint-only or per-corner radii.\n- The optional motion renderer targets browser SVG. Static SVG, Canvas, and\n  native surfaces consume the definitions but paint the final state.\n"}
